# File size & one concern

## Limits (soft → hard)

| Layer | Soft max | Hard max — must split before merge |
|---|---|---|
| JS/JSX/Vue/TS module or composable | ~200 lines | **300** |
| Electron `runtime/*.js` | ~200 | **300** |
| Java service / support / handler | ~250 | **300** |
| Java controller | ~150 | **200** |
| CSS/SCSS per concern | ~250 | **400** |

Facade/orchestrator files that only wire imports may stay short; **do not** park domain logic in them.

## Must

- **One file = one responsibility** (bootstrap catalog ≠ live sync ≠ stock report ≠ PIN).
- New logic → **new sibling file** under the same package/folder; import from a thin facade if callers need one entry.
- Backend: `service` + `support/` / dedicated `*Writer` / `*ReportService` — no 500-line `*ServiceImpl`.
- Frontend: page hook ≠ API ≠ UI component ≠ CSS of another feature.
- When editing a file already over soft max, **split first**, then change behavior.

## Must NOT

- Append another feature into an already-large file («ещё чуть-чуть сюда»).
- Leave dead old monolith next to the split — delete/replace the old blob.
- Put unrelated CSS or helpers into one dump file.

## Restaurant desktop example

```
edgeHttp.js              # request/base URLs
edgeLiveSync.js          # push/pull floor
edgeBootstrapCatalog.js  # catalog only
edgeBootstrapStock.js
edgeBootstrapAdmin.js    # categories + cash registers
edgeAuthBootstrap.js     # thin facade only
```
